+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a different reminder channel, and whoever changes pickup reminders. Reminders go by SMS
+because an email trial increased missed pickups and wasted fresh food. Repeated proposals to save the SMS cost
+prompted this explanation.
+
+## Reminder behavior
+
+Members receive a reminder of their pickup slot the day before. The implementation is in
+[`larder/reminders.py`](../../larder/reminders.py).
+
+## Why SMS
+
+From April to June 2025, the pantry tried email reminders. According to the provider's report cited in
+[issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md), 34% of reminder emails were never opened. Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of
+pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a packed bag whose fresh food went in the bin at closing time.
+
+The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone within their family and never check email, but do see
+SMS. The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025; missed pickups were back to 6% by August.
+
+Email was proposed again because it is free, compared with the reported SMS cost of €40 a month. The maintainer
+confirmed in issue 52 that SMS would stay. The monthly SMS expense is accepted to reach members and avoid the
+missed pickups and food waste seen during the email trial. These results are the reason pickup reminders remain
+on SMS when the cost-saving proposal comes up again.
